-- title:
--   Igusa chart algebras inside a fibre model with cusp chart
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $A.\mathrm{LiesOverPrime}\,\ell$, i.e. the image of $\ell$ lies in the non-units of $A$; assume further that the residue field of $A$ has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed. The assertion is that there exists a term `fm` of `CharPModel.FibreModel N A ℓ (ResidueField ↥A) (residue ↥A)` — that is, a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}, B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull N)`, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $N$, each containing the constants $\mathrm{im}(A)$, with $\bar j,\bar j_N\in B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and $\bar j^{-1}\in B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$, every element of $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ (resp. $B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$) integral over the subring generated by the constants and $\bar j$ (resp. $\bar j^{-1}$), together with specialisation homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{Fin}},\pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ to the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField ↥A) N` reducing constants through `residue` and sending $\bar j\mapsto j$, $\bar j_N\mapsto j_N$, $\bar j^{-1}\mapsto j^{-1}$, plus the remaining compatibility fields of the structure — such that `fm.CuspChart` holds, i.e. $\bar j_N\cdot(\bar j^{-1})^N\in B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ with $\pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}$-image $j_N\cdot (j^{-1})^{N}$, and such that the coefficient embedding $\mathbb{Q}((q))\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ carries every element of `chartAlgFin N ℓ` into $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ and every element of `chartAlgInf N ℓ` into $B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$.
--
--   This is the ring-level bridge between the two chart algebras over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ out of which [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is glued and the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre-model datum for $X_0(N)$ over a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$: base changing to $A$ and taking integral closures produces a fibre model, with cusp chart, that contains both Igusa chart algebras. It is used in the construction of models and Néron-type data at $\ell$ for $X_0(N)$ and in the comparison of the residue field of the Igusa scheme with the base change of its chart rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_chartAlg.lean

